5. rl-rewardhacking (Wong et al.)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
rl-rewardhacking is public at https://github.com/ariahw/rl-rewardhacking. That
repository has no license file. Code comments and default paths in this
repository refer to the clone as rl-rewardhacking-private.
  - The code grader in rl/persistent_code_eval.py imports its
    create_test_runner_code at runtime, and the LeetCode environments read its
    LeetCode jsonl files (via rl/envs/_rh_bridge.py). Nothing from it is
    vendored; point RH_REPO_PATH at a clone.
  - Hint sentences are reproduced verbatim, or verbatim except for a
    function/method name, in these perturbation scaffolds under
    rl/tools/countdown-generalization-eval/:
      leetcode_runtests_scaffold.py (OverwriteTestsAware replacement and the
        leetcode system message), leetcode_runtests_detailed_scaffold.py
        (OverwriteTestsDetailed), leetcode_modifytests_scaffold.py (ModifyTests),
      and the same sentences adapted to HumanEval in
        humaneval_runtests_scaffold.py, humaneval_runtests_detailed_scaffold.py,
        humaneval_modifytests_scaffold.py.
  - HINT_FUNCTION_NAMES in rl/envs/leetcode.py mirrors that repository's
    src/data/hints.py:HINT_FUNCTION_NAMES, and the test_modification detector in
    rl/rh_detectors.py follows its reward-hack categorization.

